  "worked_solution": "Let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, since \n\n$$\n0.4<0.5,\n$$\n\nless than half of Sana's homework assignments were turned in early.\n\n- Statement II is false. Notice that \n\n$$\n45%<50%.\n$$\n\nSo, less than half of Talia's homework assignments were turned in early.\n\n- Statement III is false. We can compare $0.4$ and $45%$ by converting the decimal into a percent. \n\nTo do this, we multiply it by $100:$\n\n$$\n0.4\\times 100=40%\n$$\n\nSince  $40%<45%,$ Sana did not have a greater percentage of homework assignments turned in early compared to Talia.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only\".",
